WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:02.800
Film Courage: Why do people fail in Hollywood?

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.370
Alex Munoz, Filmmaker and Founder of FYI Films:
I actually think more people fail in Hollywood

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:14.990
than succeed because it's a game and what
people don't understand is the game changes

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:22.439
every day.

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:24.470
You have to know how the machine works.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:28.850
If you don't know how the machine works you're
not going to get your work out there and you

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:33.070
will not have doors opening for your success.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:42.120
Also I think some people stumble and fail
because they haven't taken the time to develop

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.860
their craft as storytellers and filmmakers.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:46.239
You really have to have it down.

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:48.600
You really have to know craft.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.610
You have to know where to put the camera,
what lens to use, what is the lighting, what

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.890
is the rhythm, tempo and pacing, what is being
revealed in the scene, where is the climax,

00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:02.060
where is the point of ignition, where is the
aftermath, where does it pick up again and

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.460
where does it end?

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.820
You have to know these things otherwise you’re
going to have a really hard time making a

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.190
successful film.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:13.780
It’s craft, craft, craft, craft, craft and
the best way to learn filmmaking is go out

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:14.780
and make films.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.020
Every time you make a film you learn.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.220
I am still learning.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:21.342
I feel like I just scratched the surface in
terms of what is it to make a good film.

00:01:21.342 --> 00:01:25.830
Film Courage: I like what you say about how
the rules change.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:27.439
I hadn’t really thought of that.

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:28.439
That’s really interesting.

00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:33.220
So then how does somebody start to know what
the rules are if no one is telling you but

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.220
they are changing?

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.530
Alex: You have to circulate and read the trades.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:37.630
You have to be informed.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.180
You have to gather intelligence.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:47.210
I’m not going to mention names but there
is an actor who recently fell from grace and

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.650
he was attached to a project of mine.

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:59.560
That project is now gone because his fall
was so dark and tragic and severe and toxic.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:06.189
So the game changed with my relationship with
this actor because of what happened.

00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:09.670
Things are changing every day.

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:16.530
I pitched a series to a network that was ready
to be greenlit and the day we were supposed

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:23.870
to sign the papers the channel hired a new
person to take over and this new person said

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:28.340
“I’m not green lighting any project that
my predecessor greenlit so I am sorry you

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:29.760
are going to have to pitch this to someone
else.”

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.760
Changes.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:35.959
I had another TV show where I had two very
famous show runners a week before we were

00:02:35.959 --> 00:02:41.170
supposed to go sign the deal one of them got
named to run a network.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:45.500
But you don’t cry and weep about these things.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:47.599
You go Okay this wasn’t meant to be.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:49.810
Let’s keep going, keep going.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:52.780
It changes every day and you have to be informed.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:57.931
You have to gather intelligence and talk to
people in the industry and read the trades.

00:02:57.931 --> 00:02:58.489
Question for the viewers: Did you view pursuing
a Hollywood career as a game?

